/-!
# The constant-coefficient ideal of a power series ring and its powers

Let `A` be a commutative ring and `B = A[[x_1, …, x_d]]`, and let `I ⊆ B` be the kernel of the
constant-coefficient map `B ⟶ A`, that is the ideal generated by the variables. This file records
what the purity argument of [Stacks, Tag 0EY9] needs about `I` and the quotients `B / I ^ n`:

* `I` is the ideal spanned by the variables, so `B` is `I`-adically complete;
* `B / I ^ n` is a flat `A`-module, so when `A` is a Noetherian local ring the depth of
  `B / I ^ n` as a local ring in its own right is at least the depth of `A`;
* a compatible family of elements of the quotients `B / I ^ (n+1)` has a unique antecedent in
  `B` when `B` is `I`-adically complete.

## Main results

* `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.ker_constantCoeff_eq_span_X` — the kernel of the constant-coefficient map
  is the ideal spanned by the variables.
* `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.isAdicComplete_ker_constantCoeff` — `B` is complete for that ideal.
* `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.flat_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff` — `B / I ^ n` is a flat `A`-module.
* `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.le_depth_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff` — the depth of `B / I ^ n` is at
  least the depth of `A`.
* `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.existsUnique_adicLift_succ` — the universal property of the inverse limit
  of the quotients `B / I ^ (n+1)` of an adically complete ring.

## Implementation notes

Flatness of `B / I ^ n` over `A` is proved by moving the quotient to the polynomial ring. The
truncation map `B ⟶ A[x_1, …, x_d] / J ^ n`, with `J` the ideal of the variables of the
polynomial ring, is surjective with kernel `I ^ n` — that is
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.ker_truncTotalAlgHom`, read off
`Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval` through the identification of `B`
with the `J`-adic completion of the polynomial ring — so the two quotients agree; and
`A[x_1, …, x_d] / J ^ n` is a retract of the polynomial ring as an `A`-module, with the
truncation of a polynomial as the splitting, hence flat.

The depth statement is [Stacks, Tag 0337] along the flat local homomorphism `A ⟶ B / I ^ n`, in
the form `Module.depth_self_eq_depth_self_add_depth_quotient_map_maximalIdeal`: the depth of the
target is the depth of the source plus the depth of the fibre, so in particular at least the
depth of the source. The homomorphism is local because it is a section of the surjection
`B / I ^ n ⟶ A` induced by the constant coefficient, up to which the residue fields agree.

No compiler option is relaxed anywhere below. Rather than lowering the definitional-equality
transparency, the ill-typed intermediate step is isolated into a
small named lemma, stated at the spelling the consumer needs:
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.ker_truncTotalAlgHom` and
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.map_idealOfVars_eq_ker_constantCoeff` are the two such lemmas, and the
`Ideal.restrictScalars`/`Submodule.smul` bookkeeping between the polynomial ring and its
completion is confined to their proofs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0337](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0337)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EY9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EY9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open MvPowerSeries

universe u

namespace Stacks.MvPowerSeries

/-- The kernel of the constant-coefficient map `A[[x_i]] ⟶ A` is the ideal spanned by the
variables.

One inclusion is `MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff_X`. For the other, a power series with vanishing
constant coefficient is a combination `∑ i, x_i * g_i`, by
`Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero`. -/
public theorem ker_constantCoeff_eq_span_X (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (d : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) R →+* R) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPowerSeries.X : Fin d → MvPowerSeries (Fin d) R)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun f hf => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_)
  · obtain ⟨g, -, rfl⟩ :=
      Stacks.MvPowerSeries.RegularParameters.exists_sum_X_mul_of_constantCoeff_eq_zero f hf
    exact Ideal.sum_mem _ fun i _ => Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _
      (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i))
  · rintro f ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff_X i

/-- A power series ring in finitely many variables is complete for the kernel of its
constant-coefficient map: that kernel is the ideal spanned by the variables, for which Mathlib
provides the completeness instance. -/
public theorem isAdicComplete_ker_constantCoeff (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (d : ℕ) :
    IsAdicComplete
      (RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) R →+* R))
      (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) R) := by
  rw [ker_constantCoeff_eq_span_X]
  infer_instance

/-- The kernel of the truncation map from power series to the polynomial ring modulo the `n`-th
power of the ideal of the variables is the `n`-th power of the image of that ideal.

The `n`-th term of the adic completion of a module is its quotient by `J ^ n • ⊤`, by
`AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval`; transporting that along the identification
`MvPowerSeries.toAdicCompletionAlgEquiv` of the power series ring with the completion turns it
into the statement here. The computation is carried out on `Submodule`s over the polynomial ring,
where both sides are literally `J ^ n • ⊤`, and only converted to ideals of the power series ring
at the end. -/
@[ega "0 7.2.7" "(ii), special case", ega "I 10.6.4" "special case"]
public theorem ker_truncTotalAlgHom {σ : Type*} [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (truncTotalAlgHom σ R n).toRingHom =
      (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R).map
        (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (MvPowerSeries σ R)) ^ n := by
  let P := MvPolynomial σ R
  let J := MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R
  let B := MvPowerSeries σ R
  let e := toAdicCompletionAlgEquiv σ R
  have hJ : J.FG := MvPolynomial.idealOfVars_fg σ R
  have hk : (RingHom.ker (truncTotalAlgHom σ R n).toRingHom).restrictScalars P =
      (J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule P (AdicCompletion J P))).comap e.toLinearMap := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.pow_smul_top_eq_ker_eval hJ]
    ext f
    show Ideal.Quotient.mk (J ^ n) (truncTotal n f) = 0 ↔
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (J ^ n • (⊤ : Ideal P)) (truncTotal n f) = 0
    simp only [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    show _ ↔ truncTotal n f ∈ J ^ n * (⊤ : Ideal P)
    rw [Ideal.mul_top]
  have he : (J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule P (AdicCompletion J P))).comap e.toLinearMap =
      J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule P B) := by
    show (J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule P (AdicCompletion J P))).comap
      e.symm.toLinearEquiv.symm.toLinearMap = _
    rw [← Submodule.map_equiv_eq_comap_symm, Submodule.map_smul'', Submodule.map_top,
      LinearEquiv.range]
  have h := hk.trans he
  rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map, Ideal.map_pow] at h
  exact SetLike.ext fun x => SetLike.ext_iff.mp h x

/-- The image of the ideal of the variables of the polynomial ring in the power series ring is
the kernel of the constant-coefficient map.

This is the case `n = 1` of `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.ker_truncTotalAlgHom`: a power series lies in
the kernel of the truncation in degree one exactly when its constant coefficient vanishes. -/
@[sga "3 VIIB 5.5.2" "partial"]
public theorem map_idealOfVars_eq_ker_constantCoeff {σ : Type*} [Finite σ] (R : Type u)
    [CommRing R] :
    (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R).map (algebraMap (MvPolynomial σ R) (MvPowerSeries σ R)) =
      RingHom.ker (constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries σ R →+* R) := by
  rw [← pow_one ((MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R).map _), ← ker_truncTotalAlgHom R 1]
  ext f
  show Ideal.Quotient.mk (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ 1) (truncTotal 1 f) = 0 ↔
    constantCoeff f = 0
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, MvPolynomial.mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff']
  refine ⟨fun h => by simpa [coeff_truncTotal] using h 0 (by simp), fun h a ha => ?_⟩
  have ha0 : a = 0 := by
    have hdeg : a.degree = 0 := by omega
    simpa only [Finsupp.degree_eq_zero_iff] using hdeg
  subst a
  simpa [coeff_truncTotal] using h

/-- Total truncation in degree `n` as an endomorphism of the polynomial ring: a polynomial is read
as a power series and truncated again. -/
private def truncTotalSelf (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    MvPolynomial σ R →ₗ[R] MvPolynomial σ R :=
  (truncTotal n).comp (MvPolynomial.coeToMvPowerSeries.algHom R).toLinearMap

/-- A polynomial in the `n`-th power of the ideal of the variables has no coefficient in degree
below `n`, so its truncation in degree `n` vanishes. -/
private theorem le_ker_truncTotalSelf (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R ≤ (truncTotalSelf σ R n).ker := by
  intro f hf
  apply MvPolynomial.ext
  intro a
  show (truncTotal n (f : MvPowerSeries σ R)).coeff a = (0 : MvPolynomial σ R).coeff a
  rw [coeff_truncTotal_eq_ite]
  split_ifs with ha
  · simpa using (MvPolynomial.mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff' n f).mp hf a ha
  · simp

/-- The value of `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.truncTotalSelf` on a polynomial. -/
private theorem truncTotalSelf_apply (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ)
    (p : MvPolynomial σ R) :
    truncTotalSelf σ R n p = truncTotal n (p : MvPowerSeries σ R) := rfl

/-- Truncation descends to the quotient of the polynomial ring, as an `R`-module, by the `n`-th
power of the ideal of the variables read as an `R`-submodule. -/
private def truncTotalLift (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    (MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R) →ₗ[R]
      MvPolynomial σ R :=
  ((MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R).liftQ (truncTotalSelf σ R n)
    (le_ker_truncTotalSelf σ R n)

/-- The descended truncation is a section of the quotient projection: a polynomial and its
truncation in degree `n` differ only in degrees `≥ n`. -/
private theorem comp_truncTotalLift (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    ((MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R).mkQ.comp (truncTotalLift σ R n) =
      LinearMap.id := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ x
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, truncTotalLift, Submodule.liftQ_apply, Submodule.mkQ_apply,
    LinearMap.id_apply]
  rw [Submodule.Quotient.eq, Submodule.restrictScalars_mem,
    MvPolynomial.mem_pow_idealOfVars_iff']
  intro a ha
  rw [MvPolynomial.coeff_sub, truncTotalSelf_apply, coeff_truncTotal _ ha]
  simp

/-- The polynomial ring modulo the `n`-th power of the ideal of the variables is a flat module
over the coefficient ring: it is a retract of the polynomial ring, with the total truncation of a
polynomial in degree `n` as the splitting.

The retract is built on the quotient by the ideal read as an `R`-submodule, where the universal
property of the quotient and the description of its elements are available as simp lemmas, and
flatness is then transported along
`Submodule.Quotient.restrictScalarsEquiv`, which identifies that quotient with the quotient by
the ideal. -/
@[ega "IV 19.2.8" "special case"]
public theorem flat_quotient_pow_idealOfVars (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    (n : ℕ) :
    Module.Flat R (MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n) :=
  have : Module.Flat R
      (MvPolynomial σ R ⧸ (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R) :=
    Module.Flat.of_retract (truncTotalLift σ R n)
      ((MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n).restrictScalars R).mkQ (comp_truncTotalLift σ R n)
  Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
    (Submodule.Quotient.restrictScalarsEquiv R (MvPolynomial.idealOfVars σ R ^ n)).symm

/-- The power series ring modulo the `n`-th power of the kernel of its constant-coefficient map
is a flat module over the coefficient ring.

The truncation map `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.ker_truncTotalAlgHom` identifies this quotient with the
polynomial-ring quotient of `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.flat_quotient_pow_idealOfVars`. -/
public theorem flat_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff (σ : Type*) [Finite σ] (R : Type u)
    [CommRing R] (n : ℕ) :
    Module.Flat R (MvPowerSeries σ R ⧸
      RingHom.ker (constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries σ R →+* R) ^ n) := by
  let q := (truncTotalAlgHom σ R n).restrictScalars R
  have hq : Function.Surjective q := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    exact ⟨(p : MvPowerSeries σ R), (truncTotalAlgHom σ R n).commutes p⟩
  have hflat := flat_quotient_pow_idealOfVars σ R n
  have hk : RingHom.ker q.toRingHom =
      RingHom.ker (constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries σ R →+* R) ^ n := by
    rw [← map_idealOfVars_eq_ker_constantCoeff (σ := σ) R]
    exact ker_truncTotalAlgHom R n
  have hf : Module.Flat R (MvPowerSeries σ R ⧸ RingHom.ker q.toRingHom) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hq).toLinearEquiv
  rwa [hk] at hf

section Local

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (d n : ℕ)

/-- The constant-coefficient map descends to the quotient of `A[[x_i]]` by the `(n+1)`-st power of
its kernel, since that power is contained in the kernel. -/
public def constantCoeffQuotient :
    (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
      RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)) →+*
        A :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (fun f hf =>
    RingHom.mem_ker.mp (Ideal.pow_le_self (by omega) hf))

/-- The quotient of `A[[x_i]]` by a positive power of the kernel of the constant coefficient is
nontrivial whenever `A` is: it maps onto `A`. -/
public theorem nontrivial_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff [Nontrivial A] :
    Nontrivial (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
      RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)) :=
  (constantCoeffQuotient A d n).domain_nontrivial

attribute [local instance] nontrivial_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff

/-- The quotient of `A[[x_i]]` by a positive power of the kernel of the constant coefficient is a
local ring whenever `A` is: it is a quotient of the local ring `A[[x_i]]`. -/
public theorem isLocalRing_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff [IsLocalRing A] :
    IsLocalRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
      RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)) :=
  IsLocalRing.of_surjective' _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

attribute [local instance] isLocalRing_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff

/-- The descended constant-coefficient map is surjective: a constant power series is a
preimage. -/
public theorem surjective_constantCoeffQuotient :
    Function.Surjective (constantCoeffQuotient A d n) := fun a =>
  ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPowerSeries.C a), by simp [constantCoeffQuotient]⟩

/-- The descended constant-coefficient map is a retraction of the structure map: it sends the
class of the constant power series `a` back to `a`. -/
public theorem constantCoeffQuotient_algebraMap (a : A) :
    constantCoeffQuotient A d n
        (algebraMap A
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
            RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1))
          a) = a := by
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.mk_algebraMap, ← MvPowerSeries.c_eq_algebraMap]
  simp [constantCoeffQuotient]

/-- The descended constant-coefficient map is local, being surjective. -/
public theorem isLocalHom_constantCoeffQuotient [IsLocalRing A] :
    IsLocalHom (constantCoeffQuotient A d n) :=
  IsLocalHom.of_surjective _ (surjective_constantCoeffQuotient A d n)

/-- **The depth of `A[[x_i]] / I ^ (n+1)` is at least the depth of `A`**, where `I` is the kernel
of the constant-coefficient map. For a Noetherian local ring `A` this is [Stacks, Tag 0337] along
the flat local homomorphism `A ⟶ A[[x_i]] / I ^ (n+1)`: the depth of the target is the depth of
the source plus the depth of the fibre.

Flatness is `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.flat_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff`; the homomorphism is local
because composing it with the descended constant coefficient is the identity of `A`, so a
noninvertible element of `A` stays noninvertible. -/
public theorem le_depth_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] :
    Module.depth A (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) A ≤
      Module.depth
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
          RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1))
        (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal
          (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
            RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)))
        (MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
          RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)) := by
  set Q := MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A ⧸
    RingHom.ker (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff : MvPowerSeries (Fin d) A →+* A) ^ (n + 1)
  have hflat : Module.Flat A Q := flat_quotient_pow_ker_constantCoeff (Fin d) A (n + 1)
  have hlocal : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A Q) := ⟨fun a ha => by
    have hh := ha.map (constantCoeffQuotient A d n)
    rwa [constantCoeffQuotient_algebraMap A d n a] at hh⟩
  rw [Module.depth_self_eq_depth_self_add_depth_quotient_map_maximalIdeal A Q]
  exact le_self_add

end Local

/-! ### Lifting a compatible family through an adic completion -/

/-- A compatible family of residues modulo the powers of an ideal of an adically complete ring has
a unique antecedent.

Existence is precompleteness, after turning the compatibility into the congruences
`r_m ≡ r_n [SMOD I ^ m • ⊤]` that `IsPrecomplete.prec` consumes; uniqueness is
`IsHausdorff.funext'` applied to the two constant families. -/
public theorem existsUnique_adicLift (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (s : ∀ n : ℕ, R ⧸ I ^ n)
    (hs : ∀ {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n), Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I h (s n) = s m) :
    ∃! t : R, ∀ n, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) t = s n := by
  let r : ℕ → R := fun n => Quotient.out (s n)
  have hr (n : ℕ) : Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) (r n) = s n := Quotient.out_eq _
  have key {m : ℕ} {x y : R} : x ≡ y [SMOD I ^ m • (⊤ : Submodule R R)] ↔
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ m) x = Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ m) y := by
    simp [SModEq.sub_mem, Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk_iff_sub_mem]
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := IsPrecomplete.prec' r fun {m n} h =>
    key.mpr (by rw [hr m, ← hs h, ← hr n, Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk])
  have htn (n : ℕ) : Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ n) t = s n := (key.mp (ht n)).symm.trans (hr n)
  exact ⟨t, htn, fun y hy => congrFun (IsHausdorff.funext' I (f := fun _ : Unit => y)
    (g := fun _ : Unit => t) (fun n _ => (hy n).trans (htn n).symm)) ()⟩

/-- Transitivity of the transition maps between the quotients by the powers of an ideal. -/
public theorem factorPow_factorPow {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (I : Ideal R)
    {l m n : ℕ} (hlm : l ≤ m) (hmn : m ≤ n) (x : R ⧸ I ^ n) :
    Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I hlm (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I hmn x) =
      Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I (hlm.trans hmn) x := by
  obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rfl

/-- The variant of `Stacks.MvPowerSeries.existsUnique_adicLift` for a family indexed by the
positive powers, which is the indexing of the infinitesimal neighbourhoods: the subfamily of all
powers obtained by composing one transition map is again compatible, and its antecedent is the
one wanted. -/
public theorem existsUnique_adicLift_succ (R : Type u) [CommRing R]
    (I : Ideal R) [IsAdicComplete I R] (s : ∀ n : ℕ, R ⧸ I ^ (n + 1))
    (hs : ∀ {m n : ℕ} (h : m ≤ n),
      Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I (Nat.succ_le_succ h) (s n) = s m) :
    ∃! t : R, ∀ n, Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ (n + 1)) t = s n := by
  obtain ⟨t, ht, hu⟩ := existsUnique_adicLift R I
    (fun n => Ideal.Quotient.factorPow I (Nat.le_succ n) (s n)) (by
      intro m n h
      rw [← hs h, factorPow_factorPow, factorPow_factorPow])
  have ht' (n : ℕ) : Ideal.Quotient.mk (I ^ (n + 1)) t = s n :=
    (ht (n + 1)).trans (hs (Nat.le_succ n))
  refine ⟨t, ht', fun y hy => hu y (fun n => ?_)⟩
  rw [← hy n]
  rfl

end Stacks.MvPowerSeries

end
